<title>AUSTRALIA: RTRS-WMC half year nickel output rises.</title>
<headline>RTRS-WMC half year nickel output rises.</headline>
<dateline>MELBOURNE 1997-01-21</dateline>
<text>
<p>WMC Ltd said on Tuesday its nickel in concentrates production for the three months to December 31 totalled 25,971 tonnes, bringing first half production to 51,321 tonnes, up 18.8 percent from a year ago.  </p>
<p>Most of the rise came from first quarter production with record second quarter production of 10,716 tonnes at Leinster Nickel in Western Australia mostly offset by lower production at Kambalda Nickel due to the restructuring of its workforce, WMC said in its December quarter report.</p>
<p>First half copper production from the Olympic Dam mine in South Australia and Nifty in West Australia slipped to 44,669 tonnes.  </p>
<p>&quot;At Olympic Dam, production was affected by the planned shutdown of the smelter. Production of uranium increased to 462 tonnes. Site works for the expansion of Olympic Dam are expected to commence in the March 1997 quarter,&quot; WMC said.</p>
<p>WMC's share of gold production during the first quarter was l82,421 ounces, taking the first half total to 368,850 ounces, up 5.6 percent from a year earlier.</p>
<p>&quot;Improved performance at Agnew Gold Operation resulted from a review of mining practices. At St Ives production was lower due to the temporary suspension of operations at three mines to facilitate restructure of the workforce,&quot; WMC said.  </p>
